                <note rend="inline" type="source">352.1115/4002: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>), <hi rendition="#italic">Then in
                        France</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-08-21T14:00:00-04:00">August 21, 1937—2
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>B–290. Your 338, August 20, 4 p.m. The Under Secretary invited De los Rios to
                    call this morning and set forth in some detail our concern over the situation
                    you reported in Gijon. The latter is promptly telegraphing Valencia with a view
                    to straightening the matter out. You may wish to supplement this by further
                    communication with Thurston in order that the latter may inform you as soon as
                    new and specific orders have been sent to Governor at Gijon.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
